[{:db/id "q-74398/selection/2b4d18b815b7a8edc18986cd4de749f5c580e14db61f8b5441a0892dc9de8f26" :answer/id #uuid "14427c52-8bda-5e1d-9771-529c62678b73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74398/selection/02aa3950d01fbbc765476e8b6f3e6b82c9e3e1139e8f7f60122816dc39ab3fd6" :answer/id #uuid "f9158e8b-fd77-505c-ae95-b35316de8c84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74398/selection/14e1eb081bf1bbb84cf59dbd2865da785b7b151df752f5fed6f029beaa62481b" :answer/id #uuid "77f1fc74-be9a-5fe5-9b77-12855bceb06f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74398/selection/8afd1712aafcf0805f5d5d60dcfddddc59e85c46297a5ff72434aec6e068fd9f" :answer/id #uuid "b58dc2d6-21ef-5bd3-b687-1966b9951d8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74398/selection/90e42bacbffe27d9ecc64a10eb1c44a9692988906de7ec14d630954b5d9a599d" :answer/id #uuid "add810f6-b96e-5e9b-8930-f4b0c9094e3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74398/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "793b18b0-e232-509f-a3ab-fab10f91fc12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74398/selection/02aa3950d01fbbc765476e8b6f3e6b82c9e3e1139e8f7f60122816dc39ab3fd6" :answer-field/choices ["q-74398/selection/2b4d18b815b7a8edc18986cd4de749f5c580e14db61f8b5441a0892dc9de8f26" "q-74398/selection/02aa3950d01fbbc765476e8b6f3e6b82c9e3e1139e8f7f60122816dc39ab3fd6" "q-74398/selection/14e1eb081bf1bbb84cf59dbd2865da785b7b151df752f5fed6f029beaa62481b" "q-74398/selection/8afd1712aafcf0805f5d5d60dcfddddc59e85c46297a5ff72434aec6e068fd9f" "q-74398/selection/90e42bacbffe27d9ecc64a10eb1c44a9692988906de7ec14d630954b5d9a599d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74398" :question/id #uuid "64089810-7ca1-537a-84e6-d34fa3690e9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74398" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74398/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74398"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348715/field-1/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "3e35dce5-cd92-5b28-a495-352005bf7737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348715/field-1/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "7f143a12-9050-5856-8db5-5ee5c6c21f43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348715/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcdb6414-d340-5241-913f-a7e0fdf66c27" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348715/field-1/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer-field/choices ["q-348715/field-1/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" "q-348715/field-1/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348715" :question/id #uuid "3b1100b1-bd62-51d2-8f07-e50972013e35" :question/math-academy-id "q-348715" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/41304b7f8cbaf3df778e0f079a1651d2846f94dc74012db3b2ce936144eac8c7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-348715/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-10440"] :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-348716/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e1e3f010-a779-5dc5-ba5e-a94c70cbde91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348716/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7d59754-0374-5e91-999c-69b88bd37a5d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348716/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-348716/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348716" :question/id #uuid "e3198417-8b57-51db-a845-3bce4d1af637" :question/math-academy-id "q-348716" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/a2ccde221d71e611f7917d6dac0d12ca6b8204d9cd80a21d79005195245cf77a.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-348716/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348716"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348723/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "3c2c9eba-cfb0-5554-be09-57e67e55798b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348723/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4422bdb5-cfdd-5180-8ab9-8814273417ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348723/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-348723/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348723" :question/id #uuid "be9b4f41-fcc3-5951-9d3f-a279ae34a1a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-348723" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})={cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})\\,{|}_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-348723/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348723"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74402/selection/57505b9ef64ba2b6812de3634360a3a17e3025a18dc2a7964739092474774a47" :answer/id #uuid "c5364b71-ef57-5d85-a9bf-4984ed0df16e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74402/selection/42d69c9143815a49f56d910d8cdc8a2870fccd5fdf45621f8188f9baeea3df58" :answer/id #uuid "b0a8cdb7-8b55-5fdf-9f62-8c60c698d08d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74402/selection/07ab6c3101e11e203103f68164463047215f716e21739ab88f5f561881cc4349" :answer/id #uuid "aedd6cbe-175e-52fe-93d9-fe26d20f698c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74402/selection/644bf9a5012d61a20a0373b3af28d46a11b42da74ac599fa653b4843555e2c5e" :answer/id #uuid "2872f309-90b9-5afd-b39b-1db06b2ed51c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74402/selection/90e648cf0707671dd1e0b839fa9aa3239cb9fb68974865471dd737d267bd419f" :answer/id #uuid "09849ed7-3e2f-50fe-b708-f1b2736c5300" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74402/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bf09c7a-9d2a-5258-91ad-8a4c83e1c2e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74402/selection/07ab6c3101e11e203103f68164463047215f716e21739ab88f5f561881cc4349" :answer-field/choices ["q-74402/selection/57505b9ef64ba2b6812de3634360a3a17e3025a18dc2a7964739092474774a47" "q-74402/selection/42d69c9143815a49f56d910d8cdc8a2870fccd5fdf45621f8188f9baeea3df58" "q-74402/selection/07ab6c3101e11e203103f68164463047215f716e21739ab88f5f561881cc4349" "q-74402/selection/644bf9a5012d61a20a0373b3af28d46a11b42da74ac599fa653b4843555e2c5e" "q-74402/selection/90e648cf0707671dd1e0b839fa9aa3239cb9fb68974865471dd737d267bd419f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74402" :question/id #uuid "b03e35a1-e734-50b6-bb4d-c119df26dd8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74402" :question/problem "$\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74402/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74402"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-348733"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/b9a4695c6e43ee5ceb15ea1bbb3ee1815fdbd87e9c8b4a4e8eeba1089750ff79.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-361711/field-1/f9003861fd47f1553bcc9d156be771c9e8a9e7cd57ec294449ddcadfa2b04b80" :answer/id #uuid "60640a78-8f09-5331-a704-26677847ffbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^2}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-361711/field-1/82a873b6b3ece3b4059b2da1839886387bbd4d4e56d0ad136fc169204f9d3030" :answer/id #uuid "3bf4c878-7b92-592b-adc2-112e45c4e87e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-361711/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "859cec6a-b48c-5542-b4bf-ce49ea1111b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-361711/field-1/f9003861fd47f1553bcc9d156be771c9e8a9e7cd57ec294449ddcadfa2b04b80" :answer-field/choices ["q-361711/field-1/f9003861fd47f1553bcc9d156be771c9e8a9e7cd57ec294449ddcadfa2b04b80" "q-361711/field-1/82a873b6b3ece3b4059b2da1839886387bbd4d4e56d0ad136fc169204f9d3030"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-361711" :question/id #uuid "5028512b-a5ef-5c38-81c4-6a7be0e32b0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-361711" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/f8aa97ff1ff27ec11df6aefd4523ed9d39efac686c777f7242701aa2f4fef79c.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2-x]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3-x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+3x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-[0] \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-361711/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-361711"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114696/selection/1c373090e87b1df8df0dee8c234bf2f20d4891c44088ae7684bbe1eea1c9a611" :answer/id #uuid "5fe4ba27-02f7-5c91-9f48-1a56dab35618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114696/selection/be0eede5b75b9d4f05ffce7cb87283cb01c673e0e618189054dd9be686cbc598" :answer/id #uuid "9fae57e2-8599-5683-863f-a150d85259c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114696/selection/afadb11eff7cdc0902f9ad6a1dc564c0b12a834ab8a8d6731801baf21c823b0a" :answer/id #uuid "b4b3d3e2-ebdd-5027-9f80-9ab86295e47c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114696/selection/178b5dde2ccbe0be455f9b8cc327f59dca9c7adf24ba07bfd41e8618c5db2aa6" :answer/id #uuid "303fa97f-3d61-5184-a349-c12f8c8074bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114696/selection/e6eaa6f1d46191b06953ecdebfcdde5885921e35264d95702d8f323ef5212bf0" :answer/id #uuid "2ec8596c-f498-545c-ad50-8a9b0f32a482" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114696/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d65407ce-aa3d-565c-8639-4943b98cc9f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114696/selection/be0eede5b75b9d4f05ffce7cb87283cb01c673e0e618189054dd9be686cbc598" :answer-field/choices ["q-114696/selection/1c373090e87b1df8df0dee8c234bf2f20d4891c44088ae7684bbe1eea1c9a611" "q-114696/selection/be0eede5b75b9d4f05ffce7cb87283cb01c673e0e618189054dd9be686cbc598" "q-114696/selection/afadb11eff7cdc0902f9ad6a1dc564c0b12a834ab8a8d6731801baf21c823b0a" "q-114696/selection/178b5dde2ccbe0be455f9b8cc327f59dca9c7adf24ba07bfd41e8618c5db2aa6" "q-114696/selection/e6eaa6f1d46191b06953ecdebfcdde5885921e35264d95702d8f323ef5212bf0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114696" :question/id #uuid "5e06f254-9ae0-5c9b-85c7-9e6e4070e958" :question/math-academy-id "q-114696" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\theta =x$ and substituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {(2{cos}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the same formula $2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1$ with $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\frac{3}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+\\frac{3}{2}\\,x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114696/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114696"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-361710/field-1/41f88d47274a71c2d796e6559ccca7d98e82472da0fdd2714f2a384b156a05d8" :answer/id #uuid "840e71bf-4b19-5f77-975a-504d60b8f831" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-361710/field-1/d18a1bb9600f02e78f24b67126dbeff3638a4a289fa1abd25053ab6fa1636c52" :answer/id #uuid "cfdcdb89-1fa0-5e5b-a6dc-945460dab185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-361710/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f2e647b-d35b-5008-bf4e-9afef43b2a41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-361710/field-1/41f88d47274a71c2d796e6559ccca7d98e82472da0fdd2714f2a384b156a05d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-361710/field-1/41f88d47274a71c2d796e6559ccca7d98e82472da0fdd2714f2a384b156a05d8" "q-361710/field-1/d18a1bb9600f02e78f24b67126dbeff3638a4a289fa1abd25053ab6fa1636c52"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-361710" :question/id #uuid "aab9a792-b65b-5b10-9dcd-2375e14a55d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-361710" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x & =5{sin}^{2}⁡x+5{cos}^{2}⁡x+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[5+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(8+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(8x+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[8(0)+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(0))] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}(0)]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}(0)] \\\\  & =4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-361710/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-361710"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347182/field-1/5d122806de787172b0e9a7a89beef40d518e68f7c683c64f6c7683f16b06e1b6" :answer/id #uuid "d5dd8e22-4e53-5097-9663-141d62fb9e32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi-\\frac{\\pi^3}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347182/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d17d2d99-482a-5e96-a7f8-10615a206c45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347182/field-1/5d122806de787172b0e9a7a89beef40d518e68f7c683c64f6c7683f16b06e1b6" :answer-field/choices ["q-347182/field-1/5d122806de787172b0e9a7a89beef40d518e68f7c683c64f6c7683f16b06e1b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347182" :question/id #uuid "7e6a604d-c591-56e2-a8f3-63cd2a5f1e21" :question/math-academy-id "q-347182" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\pi )+\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}{\\pi }^{3})-(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3-{\\pi }^{2})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-347182/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347182"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347179/field-1/6568a7f527cbccabebc1d2e55fba33e6d92cc0555602b7b829eae080d006da93" :answer/id #uuid "5c9c73e6-97df-51de-91dc-19edd1d6fc14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347179/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "694ddeb6-b4bf-5f6e-8bbc-2bb046085ac3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347179/field-1/6568a7f527cbccabebc1d2e55fba33e6d92cc0555602b7b829eae080d006da93" :answer-field/choices ["q-347179/field-1/6568a7f527cbccabebc1d2e55fba33e6d92cc0555602b7b829eae080d006da93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347179" :question/id #uuid "ffc0ed13-441c-5653-8f7c-66f8bb3ae58b" :question/math-academy-id "q-347179" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/b163cd4cc1add41ae2c043b4b3d7d818dd9b23de0a4b762bc85d348c0bca4def.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\pi $ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2x)\\,|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot (-\\pi ))+2(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =(0+\\pi )-(0-2\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\pi +2\\pi  \\\\  & =3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-347179/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348886/field-1/2ee78d7e4f8d8340d5ef604ba045973e86a456b39ec4195136a815ed68052d64" :answer/id #uuid "e70fdbe2-e3ff-5811-8b25-f2fe769c6def" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi^3}{24}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348886/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb12cd62-3c0e-552b-b36a-edaad2c59d0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348886/field-1/2ee78d7e4f8d8340d5ef604ba045973e86a456b39ec4195136a815ed68052d64" :answer-field/choices ["q-348886/field-1/2ee78d7e4f8d8340d5ef604ba045973e86a456b39ec4195136a815ed68052d64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348886" :question/id #uuid "3bdbba35-dcea-5023-a028-d70a659d314d" :question/math-academy-id "q-348886" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/d1d49c23cebfe2979c8bff7b7f19d5435807a8d1aec348070aadfab1e9d2ca19.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡(x),$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1)=-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-348886/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348886"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348917/field-1/5cf956242b9863bec1345051ca8ccb3caf8118ef7c2e138f555df8faaf61abd8" :answer/id #uuid "daa8bbfb-9cd5-5ac4-af5b-f95bc53fb68a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348917/field-1/91624d7938483a6bde16ff8ead17914296822c35d7a6cea54ff66c0964b1d86e" :answer/id #uuid "97d09f74-cc14-5e81-92b4-2c27170d8852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348917/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "311d916e-980e-58dc-aa9b-6dc55aa6720a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348917/field-1/5cf956242b9863bec1345051ca8ccb3caf8118ef7c2e138f555df8faaf61abd8" :answer-field/choices ["q-348917/field-1/5cf956242b9863bec1345051ca8ccb3caf8118ef7c2e138f555df8faaf61abd8" "q-348917/field-1/91624d7938483a6bde16ff8ead17914296822c35d7a6cea54ff66c0964b1d86e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348917" :question/id #uuid "33e4ffd8-e1ee-553a-bbc6-09f216ac15a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-348917" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/07a1fab6073fdff2a20140719b570c0c40981ab049866480fbaff4dfad0c7799.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x),$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))={sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}{(x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x))|}_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}[(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi ))-(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-348917/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348917"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114706/selection/4820635fd9ab87110b9c5b1f79a1147231a407137d2f52a4f31ce348e32237af" :answer/id #uuid "e351c5e5-ab8b-59db-9b5e-19896b7eccad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114706/selection/7e9f303094813d48f539bcb431c3e4de45f5676993ad7725c49c35c6cd8a435b" :answer/id #uuid "c113ef7a-beb6-5603-95df-92ad4f197e39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114706/selection/6e9d9b2f6ef40ea91bab3e0f69430ea49b4c770a550da2a8a7090c6750d3f593" :answer/id #uuid "c5db3896-3524-5c26-a73f-323d24950fa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}-2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114706/selection/c2ccc89f7f8abf94a234ef448db521305900cf0805cf09575007903aae4c6f2c" :answer/id #uuid "904d90a7-bfff-5e62-81a0-59241dac5e67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{2}+x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114706/selection/2f08e3c206368a68472c095b3d298cfe50bc88b6522a098ee512580b9027d344" :answer/id #uuid "82a62c8c-484c-5495-b1b7-5f5850631915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114706/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "af6e7734-0646-5022-9cd7-6630c6f083fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114706/selection/4820635fd9ab87110b9c5b1f79a1147231a407137d2f52a4f31ce348e32237af" :answer-field/choices ["q-114706/selection/4820635fd9ab87110b9c5b1f79a1147231a407137d2f52a4f31ce348e32237af" "q-114706/selection/7e9f303094813d48f539bcb431c3e4de45f5676993ad7725c49c35c6cd8a435b" "q-114706/selection/6e9d9b2f6ef40ea91bab3e0f69430ea49b4c770a550da2a8a7090c6750d3f593" "q-114706/selection/c2ccc89f7f8abf94a234ef448db521305900cf0805cf09575007903aae4c6f2c" "q-114706/selection/2f08e3c206368a68472c095b3d298cfe50bc88b6522a098ee512580b9027d344"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114706" :question/id #uuid "4323046d-0eea-5be0-a5b7-ac027795bcc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-114706" :question/problem "$\\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (2\\cdot 2{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x-2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+6(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+C \\\\  & =2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3{x}^{2}+C \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114706/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114706"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114709/selection/f72bcd2c1e203a93167a4d9f63b01a1a118eaf84b818350b5a79a94c2fc18bbe" :answer/id #uuid "c679b82c-12a6-5579-aa35-c0922a857353" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114709/selection/6150c101fb24c1f32ae221232fb94aab9a1cf1c30f00036d9074d271ceb49364" :answer/id #uuid "8eeeb9d9-00a8-5f46-9313-37622780ab11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114709/selection/34ddc76d6aa24cd85fd8e6665aa18c49f34a257524e485da4b01df9090361d73" :answer/id #uuid "9c1ea649-8300-5c98-ab16-994898b76d4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114709/selection/0cecb058b8f72a4b628c5fcc08969d6eb10ee8d25c48598bca0b6ee176090d2d" :answer/id #uuid "d43de327-f14f-5993-b86b-37f87c7eb6bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114709/selection/8584dcbaf9a315d94d7041734d3150266eba72253c575d62814292b78d9e225d" :answer/id #uuid "49cc67b2-e806-56cd-a818-e2d53cbf4609" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114709/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "184b4d0f-01c1-54e3-9c60-6a883c5b3e9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114709/selection/f72bcd2c1e203a93167a4d9f63b01a1a118eaf84b818350b5a79a94c2fc18bbe" :answer-field/choices ["q-114709/selection/f72bcd2c1e203a93167a4d9f63b01a1a118eaf84b818350b5a79a94c2fc18bbe" "q-114709/selection/6150c101fb24c1f32ae221232fb94aab9a1cf1c30f00036d9074d271ceb49364" "q-114709/selection/34ddc76d6aa24cd85fd8e6665aa18c49f34a257524e485da4b01df9090361d73" "q-114709/selection/0cecb058b8f72a4b628c5fcc08969d6eb10ee8d25c48598bca0b6ee176090d2d" "q-114709/selection/8584dcbaf9a315d94d7041734d3150266eba72253c575d62814292b78d9e225d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114709" :question/id #uuid "c4dc5f61-51e0-57b7-9717-0e7b5d819bec" :question/math-academy-id "q-114709" :question/problem "$\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int [1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114709/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114709"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348845/field-1/97dfd39491b10cc6d198a11ad9323402dfba824f9b32c4f245a6b1d1f75962bc" :answer/id #uuid "a810f433-a2d7-5d74-8b19-05dd394c379b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348845/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e031aea-d803-5223-9c1c-8b78c0a5951b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348845/field-1/97dfd39491b10cc6d198a11ad9323402dfba824f9b32c4f245a6b1d1f75962bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-348845/field-1/97dfd39491b10cc6d198a11ad9323402dfba824f9b32c4f245a6b1d1f75962bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348845" :question/id #uuid "34b4dfd3-f4cb-5193-b18f-933144f4071b" :question/math-academy-id "q-348845" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(8{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{5}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(8{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(4[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})]+4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(4-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})+4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(4x-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})+2{x}^{2})|}_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[4\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{2}-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2(5\\pi /2)}{5})+2{(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & \\,-[4\\cdot (-\\frac{5\\pi }{2})-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2(-5\\pi /2)}{5})+2{(-\\frac{5\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & =[10\\pi -10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+2(\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{4})]-[-10\\pi -10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )+2(\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{4})] \\\\  & =[10\\pi -0+\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{2}]-[-10\\pi -0+\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =20\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-348845/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348845"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
